# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Working design notes, kept local
polyphony.md

# Generated MIDI
output/

# Experimental training runs. These must live OUTSIDE checkpoints/, not merely be
# ignored: latest_ckpt() globs CKPT_DIR and takes the highest ftN on disk, so an
# experimental checkpoint left there silently becomes the default for generation AND
# the policy start for the next DPO round. Pass --bass-ckpt / --ref-ckpt to use one.
experiments/

# Ableton analysis sidecars
*.asd

# Caches from the deleted audio-era pipeline. The directories no longer exist;
# the rules stay because stem_renders/ reappeared once after its rule was removed
# and 3.4 MB of it was committed before anyone noticed.
cache/
cond/
drum_cache/
drum_cond/
bass_cache/
bass_cond/
bass_grid/
bass_notes/
stems/
stem_renders/

# Audio and arrays are ignored by default, then re-admitted below where the file
# is small, irreplaceable, or needed to run.
*.wav
*.npy
*.npz

# Tracked on purpose:
#   checkpoints/            the models. Not regenerable without retraining, and
#                           the training scripts only exist at 84f209b~1.
#   drum_samples/           the conditioning loops the pipeline needs to run.
#   training_data/dpo/      hand-edited MIDI — the only human-authored data here.
#
# NOT tracked: training_data/{bass,arp}_notes_midi/. Those 7,704 .npz are lossy but
# musically recognisable derivatives of purchased sample-pack MIDI — a clone could
# reconstruct the rhythm and intervals of 354 basslines from them. The licence covers
# using the packs, not redistributing derivatives, so they stay local and
# training_data/README.md records how to regenerate them.
!drum_samples/*.wav
!training_data/dpo/**/stems/
!training_data/dpo/**/stems/*.mid
!training_data/drum_loops/*.wav
.gstack/
